    "threads": [
      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current workflows and confirm scope of SOP and QC upgrade.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 500054,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's kick off the 'Standardised Sample Handling and QC Upgrade' project. To get started on T1, can everyone briefly describe their current process for sample reception and initial QC? Especially noting any differences between shifts. This will help us finalize the current state map A8.",
            "mentions": [
              47527,
              58820,
              147659,
              526208
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 147659,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "On the morning shift, we usually log samples in the LIS, print the labels, and then batch them for the centrifuge. QC is mostly a visual check for haemolysis or clots.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 58820,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "For us on the evening shift it's pretty much the same. We check the sample tubes match the request forms. I think that's what everyone does.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 500054,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Thanks both. Are there any specific checklists you use, or is it more based on experience?",
            "mentions": [
              147659,
              58820
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 147659,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "No formal checklist here, just what we were shown during training.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 526208,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "The night shift process is similar, but we often handle urgent ER samples that bypass the standard batching. We have a separate log for those, which might be worth capturing in A8.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 47527,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "That's a key point. We also need to consider the specific pre-analytical requirements for non-blood samples. For instance, fine-needle aspirates for cytology have a different stability window and can't be batched like routine serum samples. The current workflow map A8 seems to focus only on bloods. We should clarify if those are in scope.",
            "mentions": [
              500054
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 500054,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Excellent point, @47527. To keep the first version manageable, I propose we focus the initial SOP on all routine blood and plasma/serum samples, including the ER workflow @526208 mentioned. We can tackle specialized samples like FNA and tissues in a second iteration.",
            "mentions": [
              47527,
              526208
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 47527,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Agreed. That's a pragmatic approach. As long as we formally log it as a future extension.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 58820,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Ok, so just blood samples for now. That makes sense.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 500054,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Great. So we're decided on the scope. Decision D1: The first SOP version will cover routine blood, plasma, and serum samples, including the ER workflow. Specialized samples will be handled in a future version.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 500054,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Now, thinking ahead, we'll need a group to pilot the new procedures. Any thoughts on which shift would be best?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 147659,
            "reply_to": "M12",
            "text": "The morning shift is usually the busiest. Maybe not the best for a pilot?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 526208,
            "reply_to": "M12",
            "text": "The night shift has a lower sample volume but deals with more varied urgent requests. It could be a good test of the SOP's flexibility.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M15",
            "speaker_id": 58820,
            "reply_to": "M12",
            "text": "The evening shift has a steady workflow, not too quiet or too busy. Might be a good balance.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M16",
            "speaker_id": 47527,
            "reply_to": "M15",
            "text": "The evening shift seems like the most controlled environment. It would allow us to collect feedback without disrupting the peak morning rush or dealing with the unpredictability of the night shift's ER load. I'd vote for the evening shift.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M17",
            "speaker_id": 500054,
            "reply_to": "M16",
            "text": "I agree, the evening shift sounds like the best option for a stable pilot. Let's lock that in.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M18",
            "speaker_id": 500054,
            "reply_to": "M17",
            "text": "Decision D2: The evening shift will be the pilot group for the new procedures. I'll update the project plan. I will take the lead on T1 and circulate a draft of A8 incorporating these points by tomorrow morning.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
