            "speaker_id": 47527,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "The draft A1 is a strong start. I have one critical suggestion for Section 3.2 on centrifugation. For certain immunology or coagulation tests, the spin speed and temperature are critical and differ from a standard chemistry sample. The SOP should include a step to 'verify test-specific centrifugation requirements' before spinning, and perhaps a small table referencing the most common exceptions. This will prevent pre-analytical errors that we can't visually detect.",
